ncial aid the same week as  bono's visit the government launched a  website that would be the country's main  venue for donations raising more than  136 million dollars by early july  [Music]  one key part of ukraine's 21st century  propaganda toolkit is social media to  resonate with the younger generation  ukraine's official twitter account has  been covering the latest from the war  through art to boost morale of those  living in russian occupied cities as  well as hashtags and memes about weapons  ukraine's ministry of foreign affairs  has also posted content of animals in  the battlefield to soften the image of  the military  [Music]  one of its most popular mascots is  padron the demining dog that received a  military medal from zielenski it  appeared on the canadian prime  minister's twitter feed and the dog's  own tiktok account had nearly 3 million  likes by early july if it's got a dog or  a cat  it's much more likely to go viral but  leads to this cuteness of course is the  message that we're picking up these  weapons we have the ability to demine  our country and so it's another symbol  of resistance  zalenski's instagram has also been  featuring ads like this  it shows a montage of people at a gas  station  [Music]  the video goes on to say that eu  countries that continue to import  russian energy are funding moscow's war  efforts and killing ukrainians  this post was viewed more than 4 million  times since early april  it's one part of ukraine's ongoing  efforts to isolate russia economically  and in may less than two months after  that video was released the european  union pledged to ban 90 of russian oil  imports by year end  many of the videos released by ukraine  are heavily produced like this one using  color filters  they have an increasingly well developed  film industry if you've got the quality  of the production of film released  through social media and it's much more  likely to resonate with the people that  it's aimed at  to keep up its 